{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/tbl-tm-worked-examples-table7-data","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Table","doco:Table"],"label":"tbl:tm-worked-examples-table7-data","kind":"table","title":"Table 7 from tm-worked-examples","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/tm-worked-examples"],"tags":["extracted-table"],"text":"tm-worked-examples-table7-data.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"tbl:tm-worked-examples-table7-data\"></a><p>This table records the single crossing <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(1,2)</code> at generator <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\sigma_1</code> for the parent nucleus <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">{}^3\\mathrm{H}</code> (tritium) in the tritium <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\beta</code>-decay worked example. The crossing is of neutron–neutron type, so it contributes the neutron-neutron transfer matrix <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">T_{nn}</code>.</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Crossing</th>\n<th>Parent type</th>\n<th>Matrix</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(1, 2)</code></td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathfrak{n}</code>-<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathfrak{n}</code> = nn</td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">T_{nn}</code></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><strong>Table 7.</strong> Transfer matrix for the parent crossing, indexed by crossing and by parent type.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/appendix-transfer-matrices/tm-worked-examples-table7-data.md","heading":"Table"}
